#!/usr/bin/env python3
# shelf: a game library for gom. It keeps your games with their cover art, starts them
# through gom (so every launch still goes into the sandbox) and counts how long you play.
#
#   shelf                 open the library window
#   shelf --list          print the titles, most recently played first (for dmenu and scripts)
#   shelf --run TITLE     start a game from a terminal and count its play time
#
# Files: ~/.local/share/shelf/  games.json (the library), settings.json, covers/, logs/
#
# Covers are looked up once per game, on the Steam store and then Wikipedia. Only the
# game's title is sent. Turn it off in the window's menu, or with SHELF_OFFLINE=1.
# Downloaded images must be JPEG, PNG or WebP and are re-encoded before they are kept.

